{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n`.github/mutation-shards.toml` currently treats recursive `tests/**/conftest.py` as global support, so a change to any nested conftest selects all seven mutation shards. Across 97 recent completed Verify runs, seven proven candidate over-triggers consumed 322.6 runner-minutes (5.38 runner-hours) without increasing coverage. A top-level `tests/conftest.py` change genuinely affects all shards, but pytest only loads conftests in a test's directory and its ancestors—never sibling fixture trees. A runtime trace over every configured shard found the complete loaded ancestor union is exactly six files: `tests/conftest.py`, `tests/unit/conftest.py`, `tests/interfaces/conftest.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/conftest.py`, `tests/scripts/conftest.py`, and `tests/scripts/reducer/conftest.py`. The union of all shard tests still passes (374 passed, 1 skipped in 23.30s).\n\n## Prior decisions and OSS research\nNo tracker ticket contains or rejects this exact proposal. `frowsy-beggarly-mammoth` rejected deleting a whole workflow from global support because that loses coverage; this change retains every dynamically loaded fixture dependency. `nostalgic-crumby-tick` requires support-input mapping, true mutation-infrastructure changes selecting all shards, isolated evidence, and no verdict cache; this satisfies those constraints. Three active OSS projects converge on dependency-accurate affected-test selection: pytest documents upward-only conftest discovery; Jest uses inverse dependency resolution for `--findRelatedTests`; Nx maps changed support inputs to owning/dependent projects while reserving true-global inputs for all targets. Consensus approval therefore applies only with per-shard ownership and a fail-closed drift contract.\n\n## Plan\n- Remove the recursive conftest global-support pattern. Keep only `tests/conftest.py` as true global conftest support.\n- Put `tests/unit/conftest.py` in the per-shard support lists for signing, compact-policy, and push-policy only.\n- Put `tests/interfaces/conftest.py` in the per-shard support lists for signing, reducer-processors, gates, next-batch, and validate only; signing loads it through `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_signature.py`.\n- Put `tests/interfaces/store/conftest.py`, `tests/scripts/conftest.py`, and `tests/scripts/reducer/conftest.py` in reducer-processors support only.\n- Add a deterministic contract that expands each shard's configured test files/directories, derives their present ancestor conftests, and asserts the per-shard manifest support closure equals that derived set while the true-global root remains global.\n- Add selection cases proving unrelated nested conftests select no shard and each declared ancestor selects exactly its dependent shards.\n- Extend the manifest contract to pin all existing non-conftest global-support entries and each shard's existing source/tests arrays, proving this edit does not alter unrelated mappings or true mutation-infrastructure triggers.\n- Prove fail-closed drift by defect-seeding a missing derived ancestor or stale extra conftest entry and observing the contract fail.\n- Run focused mutation selector/contracts, the union of configured shard tests, lint, typecheck, and workflow/action policy gates.\n- If post-merge evidence exposes an unmodeled fixture dependency, revert this single Gerrit change to restore the recursive fail-safe, then add the dependency to the derived contract before retrying.\n- Land through Gerrit and measure avoided mutation runner occupancy on a later unrelated nested-conftest change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The manifest keeps only `tests/conftest.py` as conftest global support and contains no recursive conftest glob.\n- [x] Each non-root ancestor conftest appears only in the support lists of shards whose configured tests load it.\n- [x] Signing support includes both `tests/unit/conftest.py` and `tests/interfaces/conftest.py`.\n- [x] A contract derives and compares the per-shard ancestor-conftest closure from configured shard test paths.\n- [x] The contract fails on a missing dependency or stale extra conftest entry.\n- [x] An unrelated nested conftest change selects no mutation shard.\n- [x] Each true ancestor conftest change selects exactly its dependent mutation shards.\n- [x] A contract pins every pre-existing shard source/tests mapping unchanged.\n- [x] A contract pins every pre-existing non-conftest global trigger unchanged.\n- [x] All configured shard tests execute with unchanged pass/skip results.\n- [x] Focused tests, lint, typecheck, and applicable workflow guards pass.\n- [x] Gerrit LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 precede merge."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786753255601182001,"uuid":"833445a8-eb4c-4276-8ea8-1221025d35ab"}